 of <italic>Neisseria gonorrhoeae</italic></article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><year>1988</year><volume>263</volume><fpage>12194</fpage><lpage>12198</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2842323</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>De Gregorio</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The abundant class of <italic>nemis</italic> repeats provides RNA substrates for ribonuclease III in <italic>Neisseriae</italic></article-title><source>Biochim Biophys Acta</source><year>2002</year><volume>1576</volume><fpage>39</fpage><lpage>44</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12031482</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>De Gregorio</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Ribonuclease III-mediated processing of specific <italic>Neisseria meningitidis</italic> mRNAs</article-title><source>Biochem J</source><year>2003</year><volume>374</volume><fpage>799</fpage><lpage>805</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12826014</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>De Gregorio</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Enterobacterial repetitive intergenic consensus sequence repeats in yersiniae: genomic organization and functional properties</article-title><source>J Bacteriol</source><year>2005</year><volume>187</volume><fpage>7945</fpage><lpage>7954</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16291667</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>De Gregorio</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Structural organization and functional properties of miniature DNA insertion sequences in <italic>Yersiniae</italic></article-titl